# oisst.csv

Dataset: cases-pier2pier — The Worthing–Brighton laser test of 2 and 23 February 2019 (PIER2PIER
  2, Dr John D.): their thermometer tables and trials, our transcription; the evenings' air, sea and
  tide
File: data/cases/pier2pier/raw/oisst.csv
SHA-256: f02b035be475aa4aa7dd20d3380a6766eab59f4f920c4d1dfffd700958b82c2c (also in
  data/cases/pier2pier/inputs.lock; check with: cd data/cases/pier2pier && sha256sum -c inputs.lock)
In the public repository: yes, beside this description.
Obtained: the answer of a public web API to the request given.
From: NOAA OISST v2.1 daily sea surface temperature through ERDDAP (NOAA CoastWatch), the request in
  the URL.
URL:
  https://coastwatch.pfeg.noaa.gov/erddap/griddap/ncdcOisst21Agg_LonPM180.csv?sst%5B(2019-02-02T12:00:00Z):(2019-02-23T12:00:00Z)%5D%5B(0.0)%5D%5B(50.625):(50.625)%5D%5B(-0.375):(-0.125)%5D
Check it yourself: fog verify cases-pier2pier (tools/) downloads it again into a temporary directory
  and compares it with this hash.
Collected: 2026-10-31
Licence: other — The readings are facts transcribed from a public YouTube presentation (Dr John
  D.), cited; the API answers carry their providers' terms (ERA5 via Open-Meteo CC-BY-4.0, IEM, IOC
  SLSMF, NOAA OISST public domain).
Sources:
- Dr John D., PIER2PIER 2 – Results & Observations (YouTube, 2019): sites, heights, trials,
  thermometer tables, tide predictions <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uJ3TLdcVNfA>
- Open-Meteo historical weather API (ERA5 reanalysis, Copernicus Climate Change Service), sea cell
  50.75° N 0.25° W <https://open-meteo.com/>
- Iowa Environmental Mesonet, ASOS/METAR archive: EGKA Shoreham Airport
  <https://mesonet.agron.iastate.edu/request/download.phtml>
- IOC Sea Level Station Monitoring Facility: Newhaven (nhav)
  <https://www.ioc-sealevelmonitoring.org/station.php?code=nhav>
- NOAA OISST v2.1 daily sea surface temperature (ERDDAP, NOAA CoastWatch)
  <https://coastwatch.pfeg.noaa.gov/erddap/griddap/ncdcOisst21Agg_LonPM180.html>
- OpenStreetMap (Nominatim): Worthing Pier, West Pier Brighton, British Airways i360
  <https://www.openstreetmap.org/>
Evidence class (rule 10): check
Where the Earth's radius enters:
- lat, lon (sites): the 15.3 km between the sites is a distance computed on a sphere of radius R
  from their coordinates
What would vindicate the flat model (rule 5): A laser 1 m or less above the sea seen from 1 m at
  15.3 km while thermometers precise enough to see 0.1 °C per metre show no warming with height
  along the path, again and again, by day and by night, would favour the plane; the same beam hidden
  under such air would favour the globe.
